{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/gnmp4jqx","slide":7,"text":"CAG works best when a complete bounded source is useful across repeated questions. RAG earns its infrastructure when the corpus is too large, changes frequently, or each question needs only a selective evidence set. Both still require grounding checks.\n\n[Sources]\n- https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/prompt-caching\n[/Sources]"}
